WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:04.270
-You're in the Guinness Book of
World Records.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.705
-Yeah, right?

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:08.274
-I think this is a cool --
This is a pretty amazing thing.

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:09.709
-It is amazing.
-What is it, now?

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:13.246
You're the longest-running
live-action Marvel superhero?

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:16.282
-From Australia, over 6'2."

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:18.418
-Wow! That's a
tough record to beat.

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:20.519
Wow!
-That's Hemsworth included.

00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:23.355
So let me be clear.

00:00:23.355 --> 00:00:25.058
My whole childhood --

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:26.626
I don't know if anyone else
here was like this.

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:29.629
My brother and I --
yeah, maybe winning a gold medal

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:30.763
at the Olympics, maybe.

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:32.331
But being in the
Guinness Book of Records --

00:00:32.331 --> 00:00:34.500
that was the
ultimate goal in life.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.302
So, we flicked
through everything.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:38.237
We even -- We contemplated the
longest fingernails. Gross.

00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:40.373
-Oh, dude,
always longest fingernails.

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:41.674
-Because that doesn't
take talent.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:42.809
That's just commitment.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.009
-Okay, all right,
all right, all right.

00:00:44.009 --> 00:00:45.278
-I'm like, "All right.

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:47.847
It's gonna be difficult to write
the essay but worth it."

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.615
-Yeah, exactly.
-Fail school, whatever.

00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:51.284
But we went through everything.

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:52.919
We went -- I remember,
at one point,

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:56.289
we were trying to catch
coins off our elbow.

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:57.824
The record is
like 194 or something.

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:59.259
-Yeah.

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:02.528
-And we thought, being geniuses
with our 7-year-old hands,

00:01:02.528 --> 00:01:04.697
that that's the one
we should go for.

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:07.133
-So you tried to master that.
-We tried to master that.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.434
-I was pretty good at that
myself growing up.

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:09.635
-Were you good?

00:01:09.635 --> 00:01:11.737
-I'm just saying...
-You can catch every...

00:01:11.737 --> 00:01:14.540
-I would catch a couple coins.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:15.841
We have some quarters.

00:01:15.841 --> 00:01:19.178
I just -- How many can you --
How many can you do?

00:01:19.178 --> 00:01:21.147
-I'm going to
confidently say 10.

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:22.882
What do we got there?
All right. Come on.

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:25.051
-Serious?
-Come on, Jimmy.

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.953
[ Drumroll ]

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:29.188
-I'll try it, too.
-Are you good?

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:31.290
-No.
I haven't done it in years.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:33.292
-Are we going --
-Like that?

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:34.960
-Are we going shirts up?

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:38.498
-We have to wear shirts.
Yeah, I mean, one of us does.

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:40.766
One of us has to
wear a shirt, yeah.

00:01:40.766 --> 00:01:43.937
Wait. 10?
Oh, I can't do 10.

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:48.174
Let me see if I can do five.
-Where do you want me? There?

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:49.508
Are we going to go simultaneous?

00:01:49.508 --> 00:01:50.543
-Why don't you
get out of the way.

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:51.744
Oh, do you want to do it
at the same time?

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:53.612
But what if it goes awry?

00:01:53.612 --> 00:01:56.782
-Oh!

00:01:56.782 --> 00:01:58.284
-I know.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:02.621
[ Foghorn ]

00:02:02.621 --> 00:02:04.757
All right, let's see, let's see.
Here we go.

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:06.159
-All but one.
-Let's see.

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:07.726
[ Drumroll ]

00:02:07.726 --> 00:02:13.532
-Yes. Watch the desk.

00:02:13.532 --> 00:02:15.635
Oh!

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:17.836
[ Foghorn ]

00:02:17.836 --> 00:02:20.740
-They went everywhere.
Dude, I have five in my hand.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.008
-They're in the
Empire State Building.

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:24.276
-There's some in the
Empire State Building, yeah.

00:02:24.276 --> 00:02:26.946
I guess I won't be in
the Guinness book for that.

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:28.414
-That one didn't go well.
We went for badminton.

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:29.582
-Oh, really?

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.183
-So, there's a world record
for badminton.

00:02:31.183 --> 00:02:32.752
Well, there was when I was 8.

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:36.755
So, if you play continuously
for 56 hours,

00:02:36.755 --> 00:02:39.658
you're in the -- And my brother
goes, "That's the one."

00:02:39.658 --> 00:02:42.194
You just have to stand up.
You don't have to be good.

00:02:42.194 --> 00:02:44.297
We actually rang them up
and found out

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:45.765
that you can accrue breaks.

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:47.099
So, that's five minutes
every hour.

00:02:47.099 --> 00:02:48.301
So if you accrue that,

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:51.137
you can sleep for two hours
every 24 hours.

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:52.938
So, we're 8 and 9,
and my brother goes,

00:02:52.938 --> 00:02:54.340
"We've got to train."

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:58.777
I said, "Playing badminton?"
And he goes, "No, not sleeping."

00:02:58.777 --> 00:03:00.046
-He sounds like fun.
-He did.

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:01.948
He stayed up
all night one night,

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:05.351
and then, some point during
the second day, during school,

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:07.719
he got sent home because
he hit his head

00:03:07.719 --> 00:03:08.721
on the desk or something.

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:10.689
-Yeah, of course.
You got to sleep.

00:03:10.689 --> 00:03:13.025
-Yeah, we weren't
the sharpest tools in the shed.

00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:14.093
-Let's talk about --

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:15.094
-Look at us just
leaving money everywhere.

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:16.128
-Yeah, I know.

00:03:16.128 --> 00:03:17.263
There's, like,
quarters everywhere.

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:20.132
Yeah. You make it rain
when you get here.

00:03:20.132 --> 00:03:21.567
"Missing Link."
-Yeah.

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:22.802
-Let's talk about this movie.

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.304
I'm excited about this
this weekend.

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:25.871
-I'm worried about this.
You got other guests.

00:03:25.871 --> 00:03:27.640
Very important guests.
-Oh, yeah. Of course, sure.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.142
Yeah, thank you.
-Sorry.

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:32.679
-Yeah. That's very thoughtful.
-That's it.

00:03:32.679 --> 00:03:35.982
-Do you want to trade blazers?
Maybe yours would look nice.

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:37.449
-Yeah, no, mine's more valuable.

00:03:37.449 --> 00:03:41.987
-All right, I gotcha.
No problem.

00:03:41.987 --> 00:03:44.723
-Actually, maybe not.

00:03:44.723 --> 00:03:49.528
-No, no, I don't want it.
-Definitely not.

00:03:49.528 --> 00:03:50.963
There you go.
-No!

00:03:50.963 --> 00:03:55.435
-Yo!
-No, I don't want -- Come on!

00:03:55.435 --> 00:03:57.636
-Wow!

00:03:57.636 --> 00:04:03.977
Fits.
♪♪

00:04:03.977 --> 00:04:08.247
-Wow. You look pretty good.

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:14.086
Not bad.
-Man, this fits. This is good.

00:04:14.086 --> 00:04:15.221
But that's a touch.

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:16.288
That's a nice touch.

00:04:16.288 --> 00:04:17.590
-Yeah, maybe
I'll start doing this.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.724
-I put all the money
in the pocket square, clearly.

00:04:18.724 --> 00:04:19.825
-Yeah. I like that.

00:04:19.825 --> 00:04:20.860
Maybe that's my move
from now on.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:21.861
I like that.

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:23.329
-I'm sorry.

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:24.630
You're listening to the longest
"Tonight Show" of all time.

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.431
-No, it's good.
I don't want you to leave.

00:04:26.431 --> 00:04:29.869
Let's break the record.
Guinness Book, are you watching?

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:32.004
That's what we should do.
The longest-ever "Tonight Show."

00:04:32.004 --> 00:04:34.440
-The longest continuous
"Tonight Show."

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.575
-The longest continuous --
-Are you guys up for it?

00:04:36.575 --> 00:04:37.643
-Hey, Roots,
are you guys up for that?

00:04:37.643 --> 00:04:38.945
-Yes.
-Yeah. We're gonna try it.

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:40.680
-They're like, "Absolutely not."

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:43.916
-Yeah, they're already asleep.
Yeah. No.

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:48.020
-Someone Google.
-They're down for it.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:51.090
Let's do that next time.
-Without a commercial break.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:54.092
-Yeah.
-Oh. No.

00:04:54.092 --> 00:04:57.863
-I can't afford those suits
if we go to that. Yeah.

00:04:57.863 --> 00:04:59.765
Please, let's talk about
this film.

00:04:59.765 --> 00:05:01.567
Zach Galifianakis.
-Yeah.

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.969
-Is it Zoe Saldana?
-Yes.

00:05:03.969 --> 00:05:05.304
-And the idea of it is --

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:08.607
you're an explorer
trying to find Sasquatch.

00:05:08.607 --> 00:05:10.376
-Sasquatch. So, he's out in
the beginning of the movie,

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:12.077
finding the Loch Ness Monster.

00:05:12.077 --> 00:05:15.081
He's desperate to become an
elite sort of explorer,

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:16.782
so he goes out to find
the Sasquatch

00:05:16.782 --> 00:05:19.685
and literally finds him in the
first 10 minutes of the movie.

00:05:19.685 --> 00:05:22.221
Played by Zach -- And then
he's got to bring him back.

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:25.158
But the Sasquatch --
And Zach is so brilliant.

00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:28.827
The Sasquatch is just lonely and
wants to go over, and he says,

00:05:28.827 --> 00:05:30.896
"I'll come back with you,
but could you first take me

00:05:30.896 --> 00:05:33.232
to try and find
anyone else like me?"

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:35.067
And so my character is like,
"Oh, all right."

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:38.437
So they go on this
trek together,

00:05:38.437 --> 00:05:39.538
this journey together.

00:05:39.538 --> 00:05:41.774
And it's made by Laika Studios,

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:43.508
which if you saw
"Kubo and the two strings"

00:05:43.508 --> 00:05:46.512
or "Coraline" -- it's all real
stop-motion animation.

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:48.380
It is the most
beautiful animation.

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:50.516
It's a beautiful story,
and Zach is hilarious.

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:51.951
Zoe's great.

00:05:51.951 --> 00:05:54.887
But this animation itself --
you've got support these guys,

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:56.789
because they're one of
the few people left

00:05:56.789 --> 00:05:58.624
doing real
stop-motion animation.

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:01.661
So, yeah, check it out.
-Let's check it out.

00:06:01.661 --> 00:06:03.028
I want to show a clip
from your new movie.

00:06:03.028 --> 00:06:05.431
Here's Hugh Jackman in
"Missing Link."

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:06.865
Take a look at this.

00:06:06.865 --> 00:06:09.936
-You are exactly as I imagined.

00:06:09.936 --> 00:06:10.936
8 feet tall.

00:06:10.936 --> 00:06:12.571
Chest circumference --
70 inches.

00:06:12.571 --> 00:06:14.239
Total weight around 650 pounds.

00:06:14.239 --> 00:06:17.009
-Well, I would say it's
more like, you know, 630 pounds.

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:19.345
You know, it's the hair that
makes me look heavier, I think.

00:06:19.345 --> 00:06:22.481
It's a little deceptive.
It can be frustrating.

00:06:22.481 --> 00:06:25.017
-Oh, and look at the size of
those metatarsals.

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:27.920
-Whoa! Sir --
Wow, your hands!

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:30.823
-Do you mind if I smell you?
-Um...yeah, sure.

00:06:30.823 --> 00:06:32.191
I mean, I bathed recently,

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:34.894
you know like two weeks ago
in a creek, uh, so sure.

00:06:34.894 --> 00:06:36.696
You didn't drink from
the creek, did you?

00:06:36.696 --> 00:06:38.764
-Remarkable.

00:06:38.764 --> 00:06:42.468
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:44.570
-Hey.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:47.440
-Welcome back, everyone.
Day 3 of "The Tonight Show."

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:48.908
-Day 3.
-Day 3.

00:06:48.908 --> 00:06:51.577
The longest-running guest in the
history of "The Tonight Show,"

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:53.079
Hugh Jackman, everybody.

